WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.879
Next question today.

00:00:01.879 --> 00:00:07.749
Hey David, I noticed that you don't use some
of the Soviet terminology that is becoming

00:00:07.749 --> 00:00:14.360
in Vogue with part of the left, like calling
people comrades and talking about things being

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.590
read in a positive way.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:18.740
Why don't you use that terminology?

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.290
Listen, I've sort of talked about this before.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.060
Um, I'm not a communist.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.060
I'm not a socialist.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:30.660
I don't think that Leninism or Stalinist Marxism
are the directions that we should be going.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.370
Uh, as a society.

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:39.210
My model is one of social democracy, taking
many of the elements that have worked well

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:45.489
in Scandinavian Northern European countries,
uh, and tweaking them and doing things that

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:51.120
account for the reality that the United States
is more diverse than a lot of those countries.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:55.910
And the United States has a lot of different
other cultural elements going on.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.380
So that, that's basically my model.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:06.039
I don't look back at the Soviet union, um,
with, uh, Rose colored glasses or in this

00:01:06.039 --> 00:01:10.740
nostalgic way, you know, in the same way that
the right talks about the golden age of the

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.030
1950s or whatever.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.060
And I just think that doesn't make any sense.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:20.799
I also don't look back at the Soviet era and
say that's what we should be striving for.

00:01:20.799 --> 00:01:24.439
So I don't know who you're referring to.

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:28.539
I, the only thing I can think of is I know
that a Hassan piker from the young Turks from

00:01:28.539 --> 00:01:33.829
TYT network has or had a show called Ajit
prop and okay.

00:01:33.829 --> 00:01:35.679
I mean, you know, call the show what you want.

00:01:35.679 --> 00:01:38.549
I don't know that that's necessarily what
I would call a show.

00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:44.229
I don't need to make reference, um, to Soviet
terminology.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:47.590
I don't know of anybody who calls others comrades,
but I believe you that it exists.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:48.950
It's just not interesting to me.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:54.209
You know, I don't there, I don't think my
movement and the policy and ideas that I support

00:01:54.209 --> 00:02:02.319
of, uh, economic justice and, um, uh, welfare
programs that work and lifting people up and

00:02:02.319 --> 00:02:06.549
reducing inequality and fixing a lot of the
things that aren't working, I don't think

00:02:06.549 --> 00:02:10.590
I need Soviet terminology to make that a reality.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:11.970
I don't think that it helps.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:19.440
And also the other thing is in general, I'm
not that big a fan aside from Soviet terminology.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:23.239
When I'm trying w I am a progressive, I want
to move forward.

00:02:23.239 --> 00:02:31.480
So in general, I don't see the world as here's
the phase we want to go back to.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:32.909
We to be moving forward.

00:02:32.909 --> 00:02:37.760
We might incorporate, incorporate economic
or cultural or societal elements from some

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.140
time in the past, which might have overlap
with some other movement or country or era

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:43.140
or phase.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.349
And that's fine.

00:02:44.349 --> 00:02:50.540
But for me as a progressive, I'm seeing us
going to something new and unprecedented.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:57.120
So it's against my nature to say let's call
each other comrades or let's do our Ajit prop

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.700
or use Soviet terminology.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.180
Uh, because I'm not looking to go back to
something.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:06.569
I might incorporate things that worked from
the past, but I'm looking to go forward and

00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:07.980
do something new.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:12.780
So I'm not particularly interested in adopting
old terminology when what I want to do is

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:19.319
actually see progress as the word progressive
contains within it a at M illogically if that

00:03:19.319 --> 00:03:20.370
is a, if that is a word.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:20.670
So that's my view.

